import
	../../html

intro-loops html[]()
	- section "\"while\" loops",
		- p quote
			A {while_} expression runs as long as the condition is {fn-true}.
			{br}
			The value of a {while_} expression is always {void}.
		- keen-runnable quote
			main void()
				x mut = 10
				while x != 0
					x -:= 1
					log x

		- p "The condition of a {while_} loop can be an option."
		- keen-runnable quote
			main void()
				xs nat mut[] = 1, 2, 3
				while x = pop xs
					log x

	- section "Condition-bodied \"while\" loops",
		- p quote
			The condition and body can be combined.
			This will repeatedly evaluate the body as long as it returns {fn-true}.
			{br}
			Unlike the above example, this has an additional log of an empty option.
		- keen-runnable quote
			main void()
				xs nat mut[] = 1, 2, 3
				while
					x = pop xs
					log x
					x

		- aside-small quote
			In a condition-bodied {while_} loop,
			{fn-true} means "continue the loop" and {fn-false} means "break".

	- section "\"until\" loops",
		- p "An {until_} expression is like a {while_} expression with the condition negated."
		- keen-runnable quote
			main void()
				x mut nat = 10
				until x == 0
					log x
					x -:= 1

		- p quote
			As with a {while_} loop, the condition can be an option.
			{br}
			Since the condition is negated, the value is avaluable {em "after"} the loop.
		- keen-runnable quote
			main void()
				x mut nat = 11
				until result = tenth x
					# 'result' is not in scope here
					log "x is", x
					x +:= 1
				log "result is", result

			tenth nat?(a nat)
				if is-multiple-of a, 10
					a / 10

	- section "Condition-bodied \"until\" loops",
		- p quote
			As with a {while_} loop, the condition and body can be combined.
		- keen-runnable quote
			main void()
				x mut = 10
				until
					log x
					x -:= 1
					x == 0

		- aside-small quote
			In a condition-bodied {until_} loop,
			{fn-true} means "break the loop" and {fn-false} means "continue".

		- p quote
			The body can also return an option.
			{br}
			In that case, the value of the {until_} expression is the first non-empty option returned by the body.
			{br}
			(It is unwrapped to a non-optional type, meaning {nat} instead of {type "nat?"} below.)
			{br}
			This is the only kind of loop to not be {void}.
		- keen-runnable quote
			main void()
				x mut = 11
				result = until
					log "x is", x
					x +:= 1
					tenth x
				log "result is", result

			tenth nat?(a nat)
				if is-multiple-of a, 10
					a / 10

		- aside-small quote
			{until_} with an option body is a generally useful loop.
			{br}
			It runs any expression until it returns a result.
